/target
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.orig
.DS_Store
.codegraph/

# graphify AST cache: derived build artifact, never source
graphify-out/

# The benchmark rig is its own Cargo workspace, so a default `cargo run` there
# creates a target directory the root `/target` rule does not cover. `bench/async`
# is a second such root (its own workspace, for the raw-tokio comparison), so it
# needs its own line rather than a rewrite of the one above.
bench/target/
bench/async/target/

# Member crates can be built on their own (`cargo test -p lgwks_bot`), which
# puts a target directory beside the crate rather than at the workspace root, so
# the root `/target` rule does not cover it. Without this, a `git add -A` stages
# a few hundred megabytes of derived build output.
crates/*/target/

# HOL4 theory output: compiled objects and the signature store are derived build
# artifacts. The proof script is the source and is committed; these are not.
proofs/sigobj/
proofs/*.uo
proofs/*.ui
proofs/*.uo.tmp
proofs/.hol/

# Python bytecode from the repository's own check scripts. `scripts/` holds
# committed, runnable tools; importing one — which is how a checker's helpers
# get exercised while it is being written — leaves a cache beside it.
__pycache__/

# local gate receipts: derived from a run, not tree content
evidence/
